/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 241 0 R
/T (public markets. 14 of the 17 unicorns listed at lower valuations than they had raised privately, despite showing several years of revenue growth between their last private round and their IPO. For the Q3 earnings cycle, nearly all of the unicorns continued to beat market expectations on revenue, yet most continue to trade sideways. This will be an important part of 2026 IPOs. Private market prices continue to expand, even as public investors have balked at those prices for several years. Supported initial offering prices show hope for a tech rebound, even if subsequent trades do not. How will these companies fare, considering public market multiples have not experienced the same growth as multiples in the private markets? )
/E (public markets. 14 of the 17 unicorns listed at lower valuations than they had raised privately, despite showing several years of revenue growth between their last private round and their IPO. For the Q3 earnings cycle, nearly all of the unicorns continued to beat market expectations on revenue, yet most continue to trade sideways. This will be an important part of 2026 IPOs. Private market prices continue to expand, even as public investors have balked at those prices for several years. Supported initial offering prices show hope for a tech rebound, even if subsequent trades do not. How will these companies fare, considering public market multiples have not experienced the same growth as multiples in the private markets? )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [5]
>>
