/T (Companies that went through a public listing in 2025 had to account for market volatility drummed up by tariffs and their subsequent delay \(thereby kicking the proverbial can of uncertainty 90 days down the road\), as well as the US government shutdown. However, what the data shows is that the year was not that favorable to tech companies, even those coming to market with high growth. In 2026, beyond the hopeful SpaceX, Anthropic, and OpenAI IPOs, the reaction to high-loss companies with name-brand appeal will be telling of the market support for VC-backed IPOs. The expectation should be of a similar year to 2025, not 2021. )
/E (Companies that went through a public listing in 2025 had to account for market volatility drummed up by tariffs and their subsequent delay \(thereby kicking the proverbial can of uncertainty 90 days down the road\), as well as the US government shutdown. However, what the data shows is that the year was not that favorable to tech companies, even those coming to market with high growth. In 2026, beyond the hopeful SpaceX, Anthropic, and OpenAI IPOs, the reaction to high-loss companies with name-brand appeal will be telling of the market support for VC-backed IPOs. The expectation should be of a similar year to 2025, not 2021. )
