/T (Now that multiple standout names are preparing to exit, another concern arises: Their massive valuations raise questions about public market capacity and investor appetite if most choose to go public in 2026. An influx of oversized listings could crowd out midsize issuers, reinforcing the selectivity that has defined the market in recent years. Though the resulting liquidity will be a welcome boon for investors, success at the top of the market does not automatically translate into improved access for the broader venture ecosystem.)
